# Exposing a Resource via the Server Class

Here's how to expose a resource using the low-level `Server` class from `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`:

## Basic Example

```typescript
import { Server } from "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/index.js";
import { StdioServerTransport } from "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/stdio.js";
import {
  ListResourcesRequestSchema,
  ReadResourceRequestSchema,
  type ReadResourceResult
} from "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/types.js";

// Create a server instance
const server = new Server(
  {
    name: "my-resource-server",
    version: "1.0.0",
  },
  {
    capabilities: {
      resources: {}
    }
  }
);

// Handle listing resources
server.setRequestHandler(ListResourcesRequestSchema, async () => {
  return {
    resources: [
      {
        uri: "file:///example/document.txt",
        name: "Example Document",
        description: "A sample text document",
        mimeType: "text/plain"
      }
    ]
  };
});

// Handle reading a specific resource
server.setRequestHandler(ReadResourceRequestSchema, async (request) => {
  const uri = request.params.uri;

  if (uri === "file:///example/document.txt") {
    return {
      contents: [
        {
          uri: uri,
          mimeType: "text/plain",
          text: "This is the content of the example document."
        }
      ]
    };
  }

  throw new Error(`Resource not found: ${uri}`);
});

// Connect to transport and start
const transport = new StdioServerTransport();
await server.connect(transport);
```

## Advanced Example with Resource Templates

```typescript
import { Server } from "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/index.js";
import {
  ListResourcesRequestSchema,
  ListResourceTemplatesRequestSchema,
  ReadResourceRequestSchema,
  type Resource
} from "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/types.js";

const server = new Server(
  {
    name: "advanced-resource-server",
    version: "1.0.0",
  },
  {
    capabilities: {
      resources: {
        listChanged: true // Enable resource change notifications
      }
    }
  }
);

// Store resources in memory
const resources: Map<string, Resource> = new Map();

// Add some sample resources
resources.set("resource://docs/1", {
  uri: "resource://docs/1",
  name: "Getting Started",
  mimeType: "text/markdown",
  description: "Introduction guide"
});

resources.set("resource://docs/2", {
  uri: "resource://docs/2",
  name: "API Reference",
  mimeType: "text/markdown",
  description: "API documentation"
});

// List all resources
server.setRequestHandler(ListResourcesRequestSchema, async () => {
  return {
    resources: Array.from(resources.values()).map(r => ({
      uri: r.uri,
      name: r.name,
      description: r.description,
      mimeType: r.mimeType
    }))
  };
});

// List resource templates (for dynamic resources)
server.setRequestHandler(ListResourceTemplatesRequestSchema, async () => {
  return {
    resourceTemplates: [
      {
        uriTemplate: "resource://docs/{id}",
        name: "Documentation",
        description: "Documentation resources by ID",
        mimeType: "text/markdown"
      }
    ]
  };
});

// Read a specific resource
server.setRequestHandler(ReadResourceRequestSchema, async (request) => {
  const uri = request.params.uri;
  const resource = resources.get(uri);

  if (!resource) {
    throw new Error(`Resource not found: ${uri}`);
  }

  return {
    contents: [
      {
        uri: uri,
        mimeType: resource.mimeType,
        text: `# ${resource.name}\n\nContent for ${resource.name}`
      }
    ]
  };
});
```

## Example with Binary Resources

```typescript
server.setRequestHandler(ReadResourceRequestSchema, async (request) => {
  const uri = request.params.uri;

  if (uri === "resource://image/logo.png") {
    // Binary content must be base64 encoded
    const imageBuffer = Buffer.from("fake-image-data");

    return {
      contents: [
        {
          uri: uri,
          mimeType: "image/png",
          blob: imageBuffer.toString("base64")
        }
      ]
    };
  }

  throw new Error(`Resource not found: ${uri}`);
});
```

## Key Points

1. **Register Capabilities**: Set `resources: {}` in server capabilities
2. **Required Handlers**:
   - `ListResourcesRequestSchema` - Lists available resources
   - `ReadResourceRequestSchema` - Reads resource content
3. **Optional Handlers**:
   - `ListResourceTemplatesRequestSchema` - For URI template patterns
4. **Content Types**:
   - Use `text` field for text content
   - Use `blob` field for base64-encoded binary content
5. **Resource Change Notifications**: Set `listChanged: true` to notify clients when resources change

## Note

For a simpler API, consider using the **`McpServer`** class instead, which provides high-level methods like `registerResource()` as shown in the codebase sources. The `Server` class is recommended only for advanced use cases requiring fine-grained control.

